https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yrCuMPeSu9s  (Capo 4)

TIP:  In the intro you form the chord and pick the notes (notes may or may not transpose).  Untransposed all are open strings until the last one in the second measure (the f#).  Then you play (D) the usual way and then (D) again with the last strum covering the 4th string/4th fret (f#) with your pinky for the (D/A).

TIP:  In the verse, play the (D/A) if you can, otherwise a regular (D) works.
 
TIP: For the line "Won't come back from Dead Man's Curve" it will start with an (A).  Play that (A) with your bottom three fingers as it will make it easier to then just slide up one fret and drop your index finger down to complete the (Bb).

TIP:  The (F#m) that occurs in the little instrumental bridge after the chorus makes the transition from the (A7) and back a little tricky.  If you can't manage try playing a (D) instead or just skip it altogether.

TIP:  The words spoken to "Doc" has one strum before each line, indicated by a chord in brackets |Bb| |Gm| |D#| |G#| before each line.  
               

